| Function | Shell call | Success | Failure |
|---|---|---|---|
| `do_mkfs(mode, py)` | `sys_mkfs(1,&py)` for `-f`, `sys_mkfs(0,&py)` otherwise | `1` → "Make File System Successfully" | `0` → "No Need to Make File System. But You Can Use \"mkfs -f\" to Cover" |
| `do_statfs(py)` | `sys_statfs(&py)` | (void; already implemented; prints 2 lines, `py += 2`) | — |
| `do_mkdir(name)` | `sys_mkdir(argv[1])` | non-0 → "make dir %s successfully" | 0 → "make dir %s failed" |
| `do_rmdir(name)` | `sys_rmdir(argv[1])` | non-0 → "remove dir %s successfully" | 0 → "remove dir %s failed" |
| `do_ls(name, mode, py)` | `sys_ls("\0",0,&py)` / `sys_ls(argv[2],1,&py)` / `sys_ls(argv[1],0,&py)` | non-0; **kernel prints and must add printed-line-count to `*py`** | 0 → "No Such dir!" (shell then does `py++`) |
| `do_cd(name)` | `sys_cd(argv[1])` | non-0 → "cd dir %s successfully" | 0 → "cd dir %s failed" |
| `do_touch(name)` | `sys_touch(argv[1])` | non-0 → "create file %s successfully" | 0 → "create file %s failed" |
| `do_cat(name, buf)` | `sys_cat(argv[1], cat_context)` | return ignored; **must NUL-terminate `buf`** | leave `buf[0]='\0'` |
| `do_link(src, dst, mode)` | `sys_link(argv[1+mode], argv[2+mode], mode)` | non-0 → "create link file %s successfully" | 0 → "failed to create link file %s" |

`mode` for `ls`: `0` = plain, `1` = `-al` (detailed). `mode` for `ln`: `0` = hard link, `1` = soft link (`-s`).

