### 5.1 `arch/riscv/include/sbi.h`, lines 51–65 (verbatim)

```c
static inline uintptr_t sbi_sd_write(
    unsigned int mem_address, unsigned int num_of_blocks,
    unsigned int block_id)
{
    return SBI_CALL_3(
        SBI_SD_WRITE, mem_address, num_of_blocks, block_id);
}

static inline uintptr_t sbi_sd_read(
    unsigned int mem_address, unsigned int num_of_blocks,
    unsigned int block_id)
{
    return SBI_CALL_3(
        SBI_SD_READ, mem_address, num_of_blocks, block_id);
}
```

with

```c
#define SBI_CALL(which, arg0, arg1, arg2)                     \
    ({                                                        \
        register uintptr_t a0 asm("a0") = (uintptr_t)(arg0);  \
        register uintptr_t a1 asm("a1") = (uintptr_t)(arg1);  \
        register uintptr_t a2 asm("a2") = (uintptr_t)(arg2);  \
        register uintptr_t a7 asm("a7") = (uintptr_t)(which); \
        asm volatile("ecall"                                  \
                     : "+r"(a0)                               \
                     : "r"(a1), "r"(a2), "r"(a7)              \
                     : "memory");                             \
        a0;                                                   \
    })
```

Key points:
- `mem_address` is `unsigned int` (**32-bit physical address** — hence `kva2pa()` everywhere; passing a 64-bit KVA silently truncates).
- `num_of_blocks` and `block_id` are in units of **512-byte sectors**.
- `#define SBI_SD_WRITE 10`, `#define SBI_SD_READ 11` (`arch/riscv/include/asm/sbidef.h`).

### 5.2 Address translation — `arch/riscv/include/pgtable.h:123-130`

```c
static inline uintptr_t kva2pa(uintptr_t kva)
{
    return (uintptr_t)(kva - KERNEL_MEM_OFFSET);
}
static inline uintptr_t pa2kva(uintptr_t pa)
{
    return (uintptr_t)(pa + KERNEL_MEM_OFFSET);
}
```

`KERNEL_MEM_OFFSET = 0xffffffc000000000` (the FS cache KVAs `0xffffffc05f0xxxxx` map to PA `0x5f0xxxxx`).

